A||N||24||V8Dreamer||Caddy 4.5, or 3800??||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||06-20-2001||08:58 AM||||I'm having Rockcrawl help me do an engine conv and I was wondering what everyone thought about the pros and cons of the 3800 and 4.5 caddy V8 swap.....I know the 3800 isn't a V8, but it still generates a good amount of hp, just not as much torque.  I'm kind of leaning towards the 3800 for dependability reasons, any suggestions?  Also, can someone post the actual hp and torque for the 4.5, 3800 series 1 and 2, and the 3800SC?  And one last thing, it's either gonna be a 5 spd getrag or a 4 spd olds or caddy tranny, any suggestions on this choice?  Any qtr mile times?<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Dreamer||06-20-2001||09:28 AM||||btw, just to save myself a few E-mail notifications, these are my ONLY two choices, I can get them rather cheaply and easily from a boneyard, so please don't post a reply simply to suggest a N* or SBC.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Cozmo||06-20-2001||09:50 AM||||I've been debating this same choice myself.  I came to the conclusion the 3800 with the 4spd auto trans. is probably the best choice. (plus I got an '88 Olds donor car that runs great for $300).  The Caddy engine is fine, I can't wait to see some results of the conversions some forum members are currently doing.  It's good that Rockcrawl is helping you, he's pretty experienced with this stuff. Keep us posted on your choice and progress!<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cozmosig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
