Z||000009||KRMFiero||06-20-2001||03:04 PM||||If i had a chose between 3800 SC Series II and the 4.5 i would go with the supercharged 3800, im not a big fan of the n/a 3800's though... thats why i am doing the caddy swap... if you have the money go for the Superchaged 3800 with a 4 speed<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>      <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||06-20-2001||07:47 PM||||bad911, You live in Zionsville?! No sh!t, me too, Zionsville, PA. I can't find any info on that site you posted. Every Cad link I tried just says under construction. <P>The Cadillac engines didn't really start to make power until they got sequential port injection and larger ports in '90. '90 was the first and only year for the port injected 4.5, I believe the numbers are 180/275. I have two of them, one is going into a Fiero this week. I have a '91 4.9, 200/275 that I'm saving for the TR replica. <P>IMO, the 3800 is a far better engine, but the cadillac weighs less and costs less. I don't really know how I got hooked on them, but I'm hooked. And I get to have a 2M8 decal and V8 rumble!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000011||Toddster||06-20-2001||07:53 PM||||Neither!<P>If you are willing to go with a 3800 go with a 3.4 instead. If you rebuild it right you can get as much HP easily. also, the 60 degree v-6 is a newer design with a better crank and durability. The 3.8 is an old design with a weak crank. It's just not worth the trouble. A 3.4 will almost completely bolt up. You need to use much of your original v-6 components and make a few snmall mods but its the best V-6 option for ease and power.<P>As for the 4.5 caddy motor, too much greif in re-inventing the wheel. If you go with a V-8 go with a small block Chevy. It's been done to death so it is an easy swap.||||reg||1
Z||000012||V8Dreamer||06-20-2001||10:22 PM||||I'm kinda leanin towards the 3800 series II with the attached 4 spd auto....I don't think I'm gonna lose too much power through the tranny, and I think it'll be worth it for the low rpm's at highway speeds, my mom's grand prix does 65 at like 2k!||||reg||1
Z||000013||V8Dreamer||06-20-2001||10:30 PM||||Toddster, where did you get this info on the 3800 having a weak crank, Everyone I've known with one has never had a problem with theirs, and if you know something I don't, I'd like to be enlightened.||||reg||1
Z||000014||V8Dreamer||06-20-2001||10:31 PM||||btw, I'm still lookin for the actual torque on a series II 3800.....non SC, anyone know??<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000015||westtexas||06-20-2001||11:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The Cadillac engines didn't really start to make power until they got sequential port injection and larger ports in '90. '90 was the first and only year for the port injected 4.5, I believe the numbers are 180/275. I have two of them, one is going into a Fiero this week. I have a '91 4.9, 200/275<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Rockcrawl, I also have a '91 4.9 in my shop that I'm going to swap into what I hope is a sleeper plain jane '87. Question: I was under the impression that the sequential port injection was impossible because the '90 and up Cadillac engines use two computers that needed more input than the Fiero could supply. So I'm using a Rochester two barrel and HEI distributor. How do you plan to use the fuel injection on your '91? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||BV MotorSports||06-20-2001||11:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by V8Dreamer:<BR><B>btw, I'm still lookin for the actual torque on a series II 3800.....non SC, anyone know??<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Ryan,<P>Series II 3.8 has 205hp and 235ftlbs.<BR>Dont waste your time with a series I (unless you get it cheap or free IMHO) they have WAY less hp and torque.<BR>3.8sc has 245hp and 280ish ftlbs.<P>Chris West has alot of good info on his page about the different engine swaps.<P>Dont bother with a 3.1-3.4 either (also IMHO) they are ok if you are cheap and or broke. The 3.8 makes WAY more hp/torque STOCK then they do even if they are slightly modd'ed.<P>I have built v8 fieros, 3.8 fieros and 3.4 fieros. After all was said and done, the 3.8 impressed me the most per $$$ spent. I am working on a 3.8 Series II right now for my hooptie and building up a turbo (mitsu 12a) system. Gotta get the old Y-pipe off and send it up to Mufflex (they did Dennis L's turbo y-pipe) and have a new one made in stainless steel. Cant wait! I am positive I can end up w/ more hp/torque than a 3.8sc and spend less money. But time will tell.<P>For those of you with 3.1-3.4 dont flame me cause I aint flamin' you. Just making a simple comment with past experience to base it on. 3.8 is THE BEST ENGINE SWAP (cost effective) for a Fiero, PERIOD. Once again, IMHO.<P><BR>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000017||fierodude||06-20-2001||11:14 PM||||when you say 3800 as in 3.8l i think of the buick grand national!!! **droool*** anyone done a gsx convertion?||||reg||1
Z||000018||bad911||06-21-2001||02:54 AM||||Hey! Rockcrawl! Gimme those engines! Yeah, ancient graymatter recalls an instance of a Z'ville in PA... (does that make us "Z- bros"...?) Yeah, noticed Motorera's post-'90 stuff is spotty now, dunno what's going on... he changed servers in May "an' it ain't been the same since". I definitely want a 2m8 decal, so keep me in mind. What trannys do you like? Age, laziness and premonitions of a punctured-envelope whirling fireball have "helped" me opt for the Caddie automagic... not to mention the .7 OD fer cruzin'... Like to talk to you about trannys, cams and reprogramming ECMs (we peons w/ TBI). The guys on the Cradle Interchange thread lit a fire for me... just found how cool my '85 F41 cradle will take the Caddie trans. Schneider says they can regrind the 4.5 cam. Shave the heads and pistons an' we'll be _right there_!<P>F41 cradle   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mountpad.jpg">  <P><BR>Caddie trans mount<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cad-trans-mt.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by bad911 (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
